A field a struct requires that no mapping produces is an error, even
beneath a struct the target may omit: without it the struct could never be
written.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	o?: {
		x?: int
		y?: int
	}
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	o?: {
		x?: int
		z!: int
	}
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		o: {
			y: _drop
		}
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0346]: ForwardLens produces nothing for o.z, which 1.0 requires: add o.z: <mapping> to v1_0
 --> 1.0.thema:8:1
  |
8 | ForwardLens: {
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^
